            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0223" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8860: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-20T11:00:00+08:00">July 20, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 20—7:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Six thousand Japanese troops with twenty-four 75-millimeter field pieces and
                    miscellaneous equipment including a number of machine guns and trench mortars
                    arrived here from Manchuria during the past 2 days; about 3,000 of them left
                    here last night on foot by the Peiping Highway. Unconfirmed report is that large
                    number of Japanese troops will land at Tangku within a few days.</p>
                <p>Japanese military authorities have imposed censorship of mails at the central
                    post office here since July 18th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
